The web TeslaFeatureFlagsPage.tsx is a thin page wrapper (its own header comment:
"dedicated page wrapper … promoted to a first-class page under the Integrations sidebar
group"). It renders `<PageContainer title={t('featureConfig.title')}
subtitle={t('featureConfig.subtitle')}>` hosting the shared `<FeatureToggles />` surface, and
calls `usePageTitle(title)`. The manifest scopes page:admin/TeslaFeatureFlags to TWO strings
(featureConfig.title, featureConfig.subtitle) with NO dataSources and NO panels of its own
("renders from navigation values / local state").

The hosted `FeatureToggles` surface is its OWN already-DONE P4 parity unit (0205) and already
ships natively at apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/FeatureToggles*.swift (the full
flag-icon header + title/subtitle + "Synced …" + Refresh button + the three-column
Feature/Status/Details table + Enabled/Disabled badges + loading/empty/error/stale/offline
states). Faithful to the web, this page HOSTS that real surface — it is NOT re-stubbed. The
native page reproduces:
  - the web PageContainer chrome: TSPageTitle(featureConfig.title) + subtitle
    Text(featureConfig.subtitle),
  - the hosted FeatureToggles surface (every web region, via the real shipped component),
  - usePageTitle / surface registration: the P1/S11 `view.opened` diagnostics on appear,
all bound through an @Observable TeslaFeatureFlagsPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the
view). No section was dropped; nothing was stubbed.

NOTE — distinct from the sibling `FeatureFlagsPage` (web /feature-flags → admin SYSTEM flags,
already shipped at Sources/Features/Admin/FeatureFlagsPage*.swift). This unit is the Tesla
ACCOUNT feature-config page (web /tesla-features). No collision: all new symbols are
